// prime coordinate x_n=(p_n-2)/501, p_0=2, p_95=503.
// lattice antipode J(n)=95-n.
// ideal value reflection would have x_J=1-x_n, equivalently p_n+p_J=505.
// define D_n=505-(p_n+p_J) for n=0..47.
// For this exact 96-prime window D ranges 0..73 and sum(D)=2201.
// D is an experimental asymmetry field of this finite prime window, not a
// universal law of primes.
//
// HEARTBEAT TWO-WAY MIRROR
// mu(p)=1.6-p.
// OAB wrap W(p)=(p+0.2) mod 1.8.
// W(mu(p))=-p mod 1.8 on the phase circle.
//
// No AGI/consciousness/singularity claim is encoded.
// The retracted scalar C=O*A*B*phi is excluded.
// ============================================================================

